'' The cleanup model (docs/plan/08 section 6). Every rule asserted here was MEASURED
'' by running a trace program under fbc -- tests/semantic/cleanup/ holds the programs
'' and fbc's actual output.
''
'' The three shapes that matter, because each is a path where an action could be
'' skipped: reverse registration order at a normal scope end, per-iteration for a loop
'' body, and innermost-first through EVERY open scope on an early RETURN.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/cleanup.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 scope imbalance
'' Constructors and destructors register into the SAME list as the defers, so the
'' measured order applies to them with no extra arrangement: reverse declaration at a
'' normal scope end, and innermost-scope-first on an early RETURN.
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN3RESC1Ev
'' EXPECT-OUT: call void _ZN3RESD1Ev
'' EXPECT-NOT: <NO TERMINATOR>
'' GOLDEN: expected/cleanup.out
